@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] mobile-reuses-production-ui
The iOS app MUST consume the same shared Kotlin implementations as Android for each
extracted feature, including its presentation state, design kit and screen layout.
Native hosts MAY adapt platform services and system behavior; they MUST NOT create
separate implementations of Pully's screens. Source: Tavi, 21 Oct 2026, "Go for the
plan to make the iOS mode", choosing Compose Multiplatform and maximum reuse.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;design] mobile-keeps-design-enforcement
All shared production UI source sets MUST remain covered by the existing design
checks. Moved definitions MUST retain their existing baseline identities, and new
violations MUST NOT be hidden by a source move or an increased baseline. Source:
Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 iOS reuse decision and android/DESIGN.md Enforcement.
